<article class="env-lemma" id="031N">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/031N">Lemma <span data-tag="031N">10.150.4</span>.</a> Let $R$ be a ring. Let $I$ be a directed set. Let $(S_ i, \varphi _{ii'})$ be a system of $R$-algebras over $I$. If each $R \to S_ i$ is formally étale, then $S = \mathop{\mathrm{colim}}\nolimits _{i \in I} S_ i$ is formally étale over $R$ </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Consider a diagram as in Definition <a href="/tag/00UQ" data-tag="00UQ">10.150.1</a>. By assumption we get unique $R$-algebra maps $S_ i \to A$ lifting the compositions $S_ i \to S \to A/I$. Hence these are compatible with the transition maps $\varphi _{ii'}$ and define a lift $S \to A$. This proves existence. The uniqueness is clear by restricting to each $S_ i$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>